      <activity id="a4e317b2-081b-5d90-855d-0edf43a36dea" activityNameId="44484a96-8bad-5d7c-9745-e2496786966f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Noise barrier wall, ribbed concrete panel, complete system</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Noise barrier wall, ribbed concrete panel, complete system
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 1db0ce71-6e88-4a31-95cf-c5e1c281dd36
1 meter of noise barrier wall installed along the roadside in open terrain. Total visible height: 3.2 meters, consisting of a ribbed concrete panel with a height of 3.0 meters. Process includes the production phase (A1–A3), the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) as well as deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for one meter of noise barrier wall. Service life 80 years.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Based on ASTRA 21001, Fachhandbuch Trassee/Umwelt (FHB T/U), Lärmschutzwand Freifeld, Betonrippenplatte (ASTRA). Dimensions based on scaled measurement using known reference values.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1db0ce71-6e88-4a31-95cf-c5e1c281dd36.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
